The NLS feature flag is computed from the PAM option instead of the nls
option:

    set(BUILD_NLS ${nls})
    set(SBUILD_FEATURE_NLS ${pam})   # wrong source variable

With pam=ON/nls=OFF the generated sbuild-config.h still defines
SBUILD_FEATURE_NLS, so sbuild-i18n.h calls dgettext() while NLS support was
deliberately disabled.  On systems whose libc has no built-in gettext (musl
based OHOS: libintl.h is an empty stub and no libintl.library is provided)
this fails to compile with "use of undeclared identifier 'dgettext'".
Derive the flag from the nls option, matching BUILD_NLS just above it.  No
platform conditional is involved.

--- a/CMakeLists.txt
+++ b/CMakeLists.txt
@@ -177,5 +177,5 @@
 option(nls "Enable national language support (requires gettext)" ${NLS_DEFAULT})
 set(BUILD_NLS ${nls})
-set(SBUILD_FEATURE_NLS ${pam})
+set(SBUILD_FEATURE_NLS ${nls})
 
 # UUID generation
